Z||000000||Predator||01-13-2001||08:40 PM||||Hey guys/gals,<P>I made a web site. I'm not trying to sell anything. It is a site devoted to useful computer information for beginners to people of good knowledge. The experts would probably not get anything out of it. I am looking for suggestions and howto's to help people with computer type problems and advice. I have a basic site built that needs to be expanded. All opinions are welcome. Please be nice  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <A HREF="http://www.usefulcomputerinfo.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.usefulcomputerinfo.com</A> <BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.usefulcomputerinfo.com/Fiero4.jpg"> ||||reg||7
Z||000001||Raydar||01-13-2001||09:26 PM||||Donald,<BR>Pretty cool. Wish there would have been something like this around when I was trying to figure out the workings of PCs and related stuff. I only prowled around for a few minutes, but I will go back.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Predator||01-14-2001||08:36 AM||||Thanks,<BR>If you have any ideas for some topics please let me know.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.usefulcomputerinfo.com/Fiero4.jpg"> ||||reg||7
Z||000003||Songman||01-14-2001||10:26 AM||||Great looking website! Haven't looked at content but the design is very eye appealing. What a great idea! I'll let you know if I can think of anything to add...||||reg||14
Z||000004||LarryB||01-14-2001||11:06 AM||||Don - <P>Very very nicely done, I think you did a great job both with the content and with the design and layout.  Good info but not so geeky to be interesting only to propellerheads.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Off the top of my head:<P>I'd like to see links to FreeBSD, Solaris x86, and XFree86  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> as well as to some of the public domain repositories like <A HREF="http://www.winfiles.com." TARGET=_blank>www.winfiles.com.</A>  Maybe some links to a few hardware review sites (anandtech, athlonmb.com, etc) too.<P>As for topics a basic primer on system security both for Windows and for Linux, a simple "how to set up your own web server" page, a page on some of the more common and useful freeware/shareware utilities like WinZIP, WBM, and SiSoft Sandra (what they are, how to get them, etc) and some info on AMD vs. Intel processors might be nice to eventually include. <P>JMHO. <P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Predator||01-14-2001||11:31 AM||||Wow, thanks Larry I will review posting info on all you have stated. <BR>It might take a bit to get all that up  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>I am also kicking around the idea of making a mainframe section since that is what I mostly work on. I have found very few sites that have any information on mainframes. I thought I might create a JCL (Job Control Language) tutorial and JES2 I/O, Data set conventions and so forth for programmers. I have found there are a lot of Programmers who don't know anything about JCL, and you have to really know that to do a good job running batch jobs on the mainframe. <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero4_1.jpg"> ||||reg||6
Z||000006||Cheever2||01-14-2001||12:47 PM||||Once at the dinner table my oldest kid asks me to "Say something in JES2".<BR>||||reg||6
Z||000007||Predator||01-14-2001||02:47 PM||||JES2 (Job Entry Subsystem 2) is how MVS or OS390 controls input output on the mainframe system. Without it there would be none. <BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero4_1.jpg"> ||||reg||7
Z||000008||LarryB||01-14-2001||05:01 PM||||You know, putting some mainframe info up would probably be a good thing to do as well.  It would help make the point that even though Unix and Windows grab most of the headlines nowadays mainframes still have their place and are very much alive and kicking. <P>And given that a lot fewer people get exposure to it (the last time I worked on a mainframe was on an IBM 4031) you'd give a lot of people insight they never would otherwise get.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||theogre||01-14-2001||05:09 PM||||Mainframes.... far from dead. Can we say Terminal Server, and Citrix? Good. I knew you could....<P>But then many people think Microsoft invented Clustering..... Microsoft wishes NT could do true clustering. ||||reg||1
Z||000010||Predator||01-14-2001||11:22 PM||||Mainframes will always be around. Just as Servers get better and faster so does the mainframes. They get more web enabled with Unix System services. They will always be needed by big companys. Every part has its place from, NT, Unix, Tandem DEC/VAX, Mainframes, PC's. Everybody plays their part to make it all work. The hard part is trying to get them to all play nice together  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero4_1.jpg"> ||||reg||6
Z||000011||pHoOl||01-15-2001||04:21 PM||||Hey, how about you put a section in there about customizing windows.  Like how to change your startup screen and stuff like that.  The basic stuff.  Oh, and for those of us more advanced, put in a section about how to hack govt web sites.<P>------------------<BR>AIM: phool88fiero<P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/pHoOl_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000012||Cheever2||01-15-2001||06:27 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by LarryB:<BR>the last time I worked on a mainframe was on an IBM 4031<HR></BLOCKQUOTE>Oh, yeah.  Was it OS or DOS?  I know DOS/VSE like the back of my hand.  After a while I would show my new bosses things they'd never seen.  Then I got into AS400's (technically not mainframes, I know) and had to learn Operations all over again.  <P>GONNA LEAVE ALL THAT BEHIND NEXT WEEK <BR>Hahahahahahahahahahaha!!!!!!!!<P><BR><P>------------------<BR><I>Chuck Hodges</I>||||reg||1
